A return can occur in the hidden state, in an observation, or only within a numerical tolerance. This interactive narrative keeps those notions separate. For background on [dynamical systems](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamical_system), begin with exact state evolution and then add observation and probability.

## 1. Follow a trajectory

Use the orbit explorer to see how a single transition law generates a time series. At $r=3.83$, exact analysis guarantees that the unit interval is invariant; the plotted orbit is a numerical illustration.

