<details><summary>Reveal the faithful-encoding theorem</summary>
If $h\circ f=g\circ h$, periodic hidden states map to periodic encoded states. If $h$ is injective, encoded recurrence also implies hidden recurrence. A constant observation is not injective and therefore cannot support that reverse inference.
</details>

## 5. From recurrence to incidence

No topological plot yields a population percentage. Incidence requires a distribution of subjects and initial states, an observation rule, a resolution, and a time horizon. See [ergodic theory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ergodic_theory) for the broader study of dynamics with measure, but note that a chosen invariant measure is still not automatically a model of lifetime human reports.

